  "finalMessage": "I wrote both test files, but I couldn't compile or run them. They can't compile until the core lane adds `UndoCoordinator`, `UndoAction`, `RequestDelete` and the new `PendingDeletion` and `UndoOffer`. No unit test has been run.\n\n**Files changed**\n- `app/src/test/.../state/AncDeleteUndoStateTest.kt` is updated. Every old case, plus a submit-ignored-while-undo-RUNNING case, now runs for MEDICATION and LAB through the real reducer, using `RequestDelete`, `PendingDeletion` and `UndoOffer` with `type`. I also added a case that confirming a delete of one type leaves the other type's open editor with the same record id alone.\n- `app/src/test/.../state/UndoCoordinatorTest.kt` is new, with about 22 cases, each run for both types, covering every item in the brief.\n- `check_r6b2.py` and the `TEST_MANIFEST.json` entry are untouched.\n\n**check_r6b2.py, run now:**\n- S410, S411, S413, S414 and S415 FAIL on today's code, as intended.\n- S412 and S416 PASS today. S412 passes because no file has a `DeletableType` branch yet, so it is a guard rather than a red test. S416 guards things that must not change. I left both alone as instructed.\n\n**Assumptions the core lane must match, or the tests need a one-line change:**\n1. The constructor takes named arguments `scope`, `execute`, `dispatch` and `currentState`. `execute` is `(ClinicalCommand, Long) -> ClinicalCommandOutcome`. `beginDelete`, `offerSaveUndo`, `request` and `clear` are not `suspend`.\n2. The `action` enum is named `UndoAction` with values `DELETE` and `SAVE`. The spec doesn't name it.\n3. `offerSaveUndo` puts its offer into state through an existing event (`DeleteCommitted`). My fake `dispatch` applies the real `AncReducer`.\n4. The fresh snapshot for the `STALE_PATIENT_REVISION` retry comes from `currentState().patients`. A retry happens only if that revision differs from the attempted one, and at most once.\n5. `request()` doesn't execute when the vault is Locked or the session epoch changed after the offer was armed. This is from your brief. The old ViewModel instead checked the epoch after executing.\n6. If the epoch changes while a delete or restore is running, nothing is dispatched afterwards and no timer starts. This matches the old ViewModel.\n7. For LAB, the undo rebase of a chained create draft leaves the lab draft unchanged (frozen behaviour). Only the medication draft follows the patient revision. If the lab hook is meant to rebase, change `rebasedPatientRevision` for LAB in `AncDeleteUndoStateTest`.\n8. `clear()` is asserted only to stop the timer, drop the pending command and run nothing afterwards. I don't check that it dispatches anything.\n\n**Other notes**\n- `kotlinx-coroutines-test` isn't a test dependency and I can't edit build files. So `UndoCoordinatorTest` has a small virtual-time `CoroutineDispatcher` and `Delay`. It uses the `@InternalCoroutinesApi` opt-in, which is only a test dependency on an internal API.\n- I added no unit-test entries to `TEST_MANIFEST.json`.\n- The shell blocked a heredoc, so I wrote the files with the Write tool.",
